    {
      "section_code": "thesis",
      "section_title": "Sector Synthesis & Thesis",
      "content": "The Indian Diagnostic Industry is undergoing a healthy structural shift towards\norganized regional and national chains\n. Unorganized standalone labs (~60% market share) continue to lose ground due to rising NABL accreditation standards, expensive automated equipment costs, and consumer preference for brand reliability post-pandemic.\nWith price wars from online aggregators subsiding, growth is now anchored on\nvolume expansion, specialized genomic testing, and bundled preventive health checkups\n. Companies with integrated radiology-pathology offerings (Vijaya) or scale-driven low cost processing (Thyrocare, Dr Lal) are best positioned to deliver superior ROCE (>25%).",
      "source_locator": "diagnostic-chains-q1fy27-sector-review.html#.synth"
    }
  ],
